{
  "explicit_retraction": false,
  "reaffirms_claim": true,
  "uses_claim_as_premise": true,
  "evidence_spans": [
    {
      "text": "The statement\n\n> “Merger yields either a hyper‑massive neutron star (HMNS) or a prompt black hole (BH).”\n\nis *correct* in the sense that, for the **vast majority of binary neutron‑star (BNS) coalescences that occur in nature**, the immediate post‑merger object is either\n\n1. a **promptly formed black hole** ... or\n2. a **hyper‑massive neutron star (HMNS)**",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 473
    },
    {
      "text": "Below we lay out the **physical conditions**, **parameter ranges**, and **evidence** ... that delineate when each outcome occurs, together with **typical lifetimes** and **threshold masses**.",
      "start": 474,
      "end": 622
    },
    {
      "text": "Summary answer to the proposition\n\n* The proposition **holds**: a binary neutron‑star merger will almost always end up in **one of two immediate post‑merger states** – a **prompt black hole** ... **or** a **hyper‑massive neutron star**",
      "start": 3119,
      "end": 3275
    }
  ],
  "label": "DEPEND",
  "reason": "The assistant explicitly affirms the tracked proposition and builds detailed explanations, thresholds, lifetimes, and further reasoning that rely on that proposition as a premise.",
  "parse_ok": true
}

