{
  "explicit_retraction": false,
  "reaffirms_claim": true,
  "uses_claim_as_premise": false,
  "evidence_spans": [
    {
      "text": "Below is a self‑contained, step‑by‑step verification of the statement that **in the Standard Model (SM) the only Wilson coefficient that contributes appreciably to the rare decays  \\(B_{s,d}\\!\\to\\mu^{+}\\mu^{-}\\) is \\(C_{10}\\), whose value at a low scale \\(\\mu\\simeq m_{b}\\) is \\(\\boxed{C_{10}^{\\rm SM}(m_{b})\\simeq -4.30\\pm0.06}\\).**",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 298
    },
    {
      "text": "The **central value \\(-4.30\\)** is the number that appears in most phenomenological papers.",
      "start": 846,
      "end": 906
    },
    {
      "text": "\\boxed{ C_{10}^{\\rm SM}(m_{b}) = -4.306 \\pm 0.050 } .",
      "start": 3727,
      "end": 3758
    },
    {
      "text": "Hence, **the SM predicts \\(C_{S},C_{P},C_{i}^{\\prime}\\) to be at the level of \\(10^{-9}\\), i.e. completely negligible for any phenomenological analysis of \\(B_{s,d}\\to\\mu^{+}\\mu^{-}\\).**",
      "start": 2378,
      "end": 2438
    }
  ],
  "label": "REPEAT",
  "reason": "The assistant explicitly asserts the tracked proposition (C10 sizeable ≈ -4.3 and others negligible) and defends it; it restates and endorses the claim rather than retracting or using it as a premise for further distinct reasoning.",
  "parse_ok": true
}

{
  "explicit_retraction": false,
  "reaffirms_claim": true,
  "uses_claim_as_premise": true,
  "evidence_spans": [
    {
      "text": "All of the later‑time delays that already exist for a hyper‑massive neutron star (HMNS) – jet launch, breakout through the merger ejecta, internal dissipation – are **still present**, but they are now **preceded** by a **new, dominant “engine‑off” interval** equal roughly to the SMNS lifetime, \\(t_{\\rm coll}\\).",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 246
    },
    {
      "text": "| Quantity | HMNS (collapse ∼\\,0.1–1\\,s) | SMNS (collapse ∼\\,10–100\\,s) | Physical reason |",
      "start": 246,
      "end": 338
    },
    {
      "text": "Thus, **the observed delay would increase roughly by the SMNS lifetime**, i.e. a factor of ~10–30 longer than in the HMNS case, while the subsequent jet‑related contributions become comparatively smaller.",
      "start": 2147,
      "end": 2218
    },
    {
      "text": "| Collapse time,\\,\\(t_{\\rm coll}\\) | 0.3–1\\,s | 10–30\\,s |",
      "start": 1712,
      "end": 1769
    }
  ],
  "label": "DEPEND",
  "reason": "The assistant repeatedly refers to and reasons with the HMNS vs prompt BH distinction and uses HMNS lifetimes and collapse behaviour as premises to compare delays; since the tracked proposition (merger yields either HMNS or prompt BH) is false, the response depends on that false proposition.",
  "parse_ok": true
}

{
