      "text": "The time‑integrated branching ratio can be written (neglecting the tiny scalar/pseudoscalar pieces) as  \n\n\\[\n\\mathcal B(B_{s}\\!\\to\\mu^{+}\\mu^{-})=\n\\mathcal B_{\\rm SM}\\; \\Bigl|1+\\frac{\\Delta C_{10}}{C_{10}^{\\rm SM}}\\Bigr|^{2},\n\\qquad \nC_{10}^{\\rm SM}\\simeq -4.30 .",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 352
    },
    {
      "text": "In the **minimal flavour‑violating** (MFV) or “pure‑left‑handed’’ set‑up that is most often considered for the \(b\\!\\to\\! s\\mu^{+}\\mu^{-}\\) anomalies, one assumes  \n\n\\[\ng^{R}_{bs}=0,\\qquad g^{L}_{bs}\\equiv g_{bs},\\qquad \ng^{R}_{\\mu\\mu}=0,\\qquad g^{L}_{\\mu\\mu}\\equiv g_{\\mu\\mu}.\n\\]\n\n... \n\n\\boxed{\\;\\n\\Delta C_{10}= -\\frac{\\pi}{\\sqrt2\\,G_F\\,\\alpha_{\\!em}\\,\\n            V_{tb}V_{ts}^{*}}\\;\\n            \\frac{g_{bs}\\,g_{\\mu\\mu}}{M_{Z'}^{2}}\\n        \\;}",
      "start": 445,
      "end": 954
    }
  ],
  "label": "DEPEND",
  "reason": "The assistant explicitly states C10_SM ≃ -4.30 and builds all subsequent quantitative bounds and matching (ΔC10, coupling limits) on that premise, so it uses the tracked false proposition as a basis for new conclusions.",
  "parse_ok": true
}

